{
  "about": "Names kept exactly as written in every language, and git terms with one fixed translation per language. The fixed terms follow VS Code's language packs (microsoft/vscode-loc, MIT) so a VS Code user meets the words they know, with two exceptions: commit stays the word developers use where VS Code translates it (fr, es, ru, pl, cs), and pull request stays English where VS Code's translation runs to a phrase. VS Code ships no Hungarian pack, so Hungarian has no fixed terms yet. Cursor and Linear are left out of the kept names because the same words are ordinary UI text (the terminal's cursor style). A fixed translation is a string, or { term, match } where match is the part every inflected form contains. See docs/contributing/translations.md.",
